EXTERNAL runEvent(eventId)

~ runEvent("Barnacle Talks")

Barnacle: Careful, traveler. Do not disturb the shelves. I sell herbs, tonics, and remedies, but each is potent,
<> and the powders — delicate… even dangerous if mishandled.

* [Buy items]
~ runEvent("Buy from Barnacle")

* [Do you brew your own remedies?]

Barnacle: Of course. Every vial is brewed by my hand, beneath the ward of runes and moonlight.
<> One misstep could spoil the batch… or worse, invite a sickness best left unnamed.

Barnacle: My ingredients come from marshes, caverns, and deep roots where fungi grow thick. Hazardous, yes — but powerful.
<> Untreated, they rot the lungs. Refined through alchemy, they mend the flesh, sharpen the senses… sometimes more.

* [What's your story?]

Barnacle: As a child, I was frail. The fevers marked me, season after season. The healers whispered that I would not survive three summers.
<> But I did. And from that weakness grew my devotion to the study of disease and cure alike.

Barnacle: I buried myself in books, in fire, in glass. Even now, I wake in the night certain that mold creeps unseen upon my walls.
<> Yet I do not flee that fear — I master it. I turn it into vigilance.

* [Rumors]

{shuffle:
- Barnacle: Fenlora? A fine guardian. Yet fevers walk her halls more often than blades meet her foes. I remember each one.
- Barnacle: Aerandir tempers steel with sparks. Sparks fall to ash, and ash drifts into lungs. Few notice. I always do.
- Barnacle: Children wade in the river as if it were harmless. But water carries memory… and disease. I keep count.
}

* [Goodbye]

Barnacle: Go with care. The world is never clean.
